From 332d1ff9e8ca93b80498d32882b9f69e1bfcf289 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:41:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] S3-1: a new relationship slots into the sorted edge
 table with a halfword move on the GBA

With the pass spread, the heaviest resident updates are the ones that create a bond: rel_get_or_add
moved ~4.6 KB (1,500 of the 2,048 edges, 6-byte records on 2-byte boundaries) with libc memmove, which
copies such a block byte by byte: 3-7 ms inside one tick, a 50 ms frame on a screen already near its
budget (2.4% of the ticks of a default-clock town gain an edge). edges_open_gap moves halfwords, four
a round, from the top down: the hub's worst resident tick 6.8 -> 3.2 ms (GBA, hub light ticks), the shop
window's 15 frames over 33 ms -> 0. GBA only (DOOMO_PLATFORM_GBA) and in the host tests
(DOOMO_EDGE_GAP_LOOP in core/Makefile, so the loop is what test_town checks); PS1, Dreamcast and the
other builds keep memmove: no change there. test_town: random pairs in random order against a plain
sorted reference table (fails if one halfword is wrong).

cross-stream: core/Makefile (one define for the host build).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
